      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14169002/assets/752bdd55a25b4949fc12ef1ddc68d57f3018617bbbbfd25812c664db606ae53f.png)\n\nThe perimeter $p$ of the equilateral triangle $△ABC$ is $18$ and the perimeter ${p}_{1}$ of the isosceles triangle $△ACD$ is $14.$ What is the measure of $\\overset{―}{AD}?$",
      "worked_solution": "We're told that the perimeter of $△ABC$ is $p=18,$ and since all $3$ sides have equal length,  we get\n\n$$\nAC=\\frac{p}{3}=\\frac{18}{3}=6.\n$$\n\nFor the perimeter ${p}_{1}$ of the isosceles triangle $△ACD,$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{p}_{1} & =AC+CD+AD \\\\ 14 & =AC+2AD \\\\ 14 & =6+2AD \\\\ 8 & =2AD \\\\ AD & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
